{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Am I instead of Elohim?</b> Since Rachel said, 'You should have prayed for me,' and Jacob answered her, 'Is it for this that you said, \"Give me children\"?' — the implication, in any case, is: And am I so confident that HaShem will accept my prayer? For perhaps sin will cause HaShem to screen with a cloud, preventing the prayer from passing through. For everyone whose prayer is accepted is like one who stands literally underneath Elohim, with nothing at all interposing between him and Elohim; but when his prayer is not heard, it is as though there is a screen that separates and interposes between him and Elohim, as it is written (Lamentations 3:44), ״סַכּוֹתָ בֶעָנָן לָךְ מֵעֲבוֹר תְּפִלָּה״ — 'You screen Yourself with a cloud, that prayer should not pass through.' And this cloud is the dark matter upon which every dispute and every affliction depends, as it is written (Isaiah 59:2), ״עֲוֹנוֹתֵיכֶם הָיוּ מַבְדִּילִין בֵּינֵיכֶם לְבֵין אֱלֹהֵיכֶם״ — 'Your iniquities have become separating between you and your Elohim.' And therefore he said, 'who has withheld from you fruit of the womb' — for since He withheld from you and not from me, if so, HaShem certainly knows that there is some sin in you that caused the withholding of fruit of the womb from you, and that sin will without doubt screen the prayer from passing through. Immediately Rachel set her heart to search through her deeds — what sin she had committed — and she found nothing except the trait of jealousy that was in her, as it is stated (Genesis 30:1), ״וַתְּקַנֵּא רָחֵל בַּאֲחוֹתָהּ״ — 'And Rachel was jealous of her sister.' And she thought that this sin had caused Jacob's prayer to be of no avail. She therefore set her heart to return in repentance, to incline toward the opposite extreme in the very matter in which she had sinned — namely, that at first she was jealous even of her sister, and afterward she was not jealous even of her maidservant. Therefore she said that in the merit of bringing my rival into my house, I too will be built up through her.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:15.956273606Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}